invariant: INV-4
file: rand_draw.h
catches: tcp_blocking_loop_session
reason: rand_draw calls the source without writing zero first, so a source
  that returns without writing leaves the bytes the buffer held. The draw
  sites check for zeros, and a stack buffer's old bytes pass that check,
  then go to the peer as an RSA-PSS salt or a ServerHello random.
  test/tcp_blocking_session_tests.h draws into 0xa5 bytes from a source
  that writes nothing and requires zeros.

--- old
    ct_wipe(p, n);
#ifdef CH_RAND_SESSION
--- new
#ifdef CH_RAND_SESSION
